# COBRA RETREATS (John 13 Nov 2026 22:44-22:50). Stock X-COM aliens almost never retreat; Cobra does.
# Breaking is a CHANCE, rolled at the end of each Joe turn (John 23:20: a fixed line was "to stiff"):
#   - losses: 0% while fewer than breakFrom% of its men are down/dead/gone, rising to 100% at breakAt%
#   - + leaderDownAdd% while its leader is down (rank STR_LIVE_LEADER / STR_LIVE_COMMANDER: officers, villains)
#   - + outnumberedAdd% while the Joes it can see this turn >= `outnumbered` times its men still standing
#   - certain once it has what it came for (a Cobra man is carrying off a knocked-out Joe)
# Once broken it stays broken, and the battle shows "COBRA IS PULLING OUT".
# How they go depends on the man (John 22:50): troopers (STR_LIVE_SOLDIER / STR_LIVE_TERRORIST) run for
# the nearest map edge without firing; officers and villains take the cheapest shot their weapon has at the
# nearest Joe in sight, once a turn, then pull back (John 23:20); the unit types in neverRetreat (B.A.T.s)
# never leave.
# A man who reaches the map edge on Cobra's turn is gone: not killed, not captured, no corpse. He counts
# as a Cobra survivor (the Joes he saw get +1 on Cobra's file). When the last of them is gone the Joes
# hold the field: a win, and they keep whatever is on the map (John 22:48), but the win earns
# winGoodwillCut less goodwill in that country (and less public confidence once G.I. Joe is public).
# The debriefing lists "Cobra men who got away".
# NOT YET: they head for the nearest edge, not their own vehicle or the edge they came in by; nobody
# deliberately stays behind as a rear guard. Every number is BUILD's first pass.

retreat:
  breakFrom: 25
  breakAt: 75
  leaderDownAdd: 40
  outnumbered: 2
  outnumberedAdd: 30
  winGoodwillCut: 1
  neverRetreat:
    - STR_BAT_TERRORIST

extraStrings:
  - type: en-US
    strings: &rtstr
      STR_COBRA_PULLING_OUT: "COBRA IS PULLING OUT"
      STR_COBRA_GOT_AWAY: "Cobra men who got away"
  - type: en-GB
    strings: *rtstr
